2. EXECUTIVE EDGE MAP

- TrueForge is a serious new open-source agent-harness candidate:
created 2026-07-23, pushed today, 5,722 stars / 441 forks live. It
packages model calls, MCP, skills, sandboxing, approvals,
context/session state, subagents and UI/API into a vendor-neutral
runtime. This is much closer to the emerging agent operating layer
than another thin framework.

- OpenMontage is the strongest autonomous-media object found so far:
an open-source agentic video-production system with 12 pipelines, 100+
tools and 700+ skill/production-knowledge files. Live GitHub: 59,690
stars / 7,513 forks. It can run under Claude Code, Codex or OpenCode
and supports local/open paths as well as paid generation.

- Uber ADR is the most important defender object found this pass
because it is not merely a scanner: it captures agent intent/tool
traces, discovers agent/MCP surfaces, benchmarks attacks and performs
two-tier runtime detection. It is production-proven at Uber and its
benchmark covers 300+ tasks and 134 MCP servers.

- Tripwire is the opposite end of the signal spectrum: only 10 stars /
2 forks, but created Aug 1 and specifically targets sandboxed
pre-install scanning of AI skills + MCP servers with a fail-closed
guard. Low adoption, useful mechanism; WATCH rather than endorse.

